.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="De Moivre (1733) showed that the binomial distribution, suitably standardized, approaches the normal curve for large n. Laplace (1810) extended this to sums of many independent variables of almost any distribution: the standardized mean Z = (\bar X_n - \mu)/(\sigma/\sqrt n) tends to \mathcal N(0, 1), whatever the shape of the summands.">

